<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Petrović-Njegoš</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Petrović-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petar-ii-petrovic-njegos">Njegoš</a> ruled Montenegro from 1696 to 1918, first as prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> passing the office from uncle to nephew and, from 1852, as secular princes. Nikola I took the title of king in 1910. The dynasty was deposed when Montenegro was united with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-petrovic-njegos.jpg" alt="House of Petrović-Njegoš" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Type a rule This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_Petrovi%C4%87-Njego%C5%A1_(alt).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
